Strong Final Interview Answer

Snowflake billing consists of compute, storage, and data transfer charges. Compute costs are measured using Snowflake credits and include Virtual Warehouses, Cloud Services, and Serverless Features. Virtual Warehouse billing depends on warehouse size and runtime, while suspended warehouses consume no credits. Cloud Services support metadata and optimization operations, with charges waived up to 10% of daily warehouse compute usage. Serverless features like Snowpipe and Automatic Clustering are fully managed by Snowflake. Storage and data transfer are billed separately using flat currency-based pricing.
